# David DJ Roy — Project Rules

## Client
- Stage / public name: **David D.J. Roy** (also David DJ Roy)
- Roles: stand-up comedian, storyteller, spoken word artist, actor, booker
- Based in: Canada (list as Canadian; do not pin a city)
- Came up in: Vancouver arts / comedy / slam (credits stay historical)

## Stack (STRICT)
- Vanilla HTML5 + Vanilla JS + Tailwind via CDN only
- No Node, npm, React, bundlers, or build tools
- Vanilla site: `index.html` with section anchors (`#kit`, `#about`, `#media`, `#merch`, `#book`) plus printable `kit.html` one-sheet

## Brand
- Vibe: gritty, raw, engaging; dark and light storytelling
- Do not copy Dickie Lakeshore colors, type, or copy
- Colors: stage `#0c0a09`, bone `#e8e0d4`, rust `#c45c26`
- Type: Bebas Neue (display), IBM Plex Sans (body)

## Booking
- Public address lives in **one** constant: `BOOKING_EMAIL` in `app.js`
- Keep JSON-LD / mailto markup in sync when that address changes
- Form builds a `mailto:` for venues, casting, media, comedians, and other inquiries
- Live inbox: `Daviddjroy@gmail.com`

## Content
- Source of truth: `david_dj_roy_background.txt`
- Use the exact links from that file; do not invent social URLs, quotes, or show dates
- TikTok / Facebook / X: no URLs on file — send people to Linktree, do not invent handles
- Merch is the Spring store (outbound link), not in-person-only

## SEO
- Canonical / OG URL: `https://daviddjroy.com/`
- Keep Open Graph, Twitter Card, and JSON-LD `Person` in sync when contact/socials change
- Favicon: `img/favicon.svg`
- Live stills from David's own YouTube clips live in `img/still-*.jpg`; `img/hero.jpg` is the slam still for Open Graph
- Do not invent headshots; replace stills only with photos David provides
